WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.112
First: why does Gate 5
cover incidents only?

3
00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:06.337
The answer is b.

4
00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:09.050
The A P I's event category has one value,

5
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.288
incident, and planned
maintenance isn't in it.

6
00:00:12.288 --> 00:00:15.762
It isn't the kit filtering
anything, and it isn't the role.

7
00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:20.837
Second: a workload is in an Assured
Workloads FedRAMP Moderate package.

8
00:00:20.837 --> 00:00:22.312
What does the agency do?

9
00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:23.238
The answer is b.

10
00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:25.013
Record the gap with the ISSO.

11
00:00:25.013 --> 00:00:29.874
Personalized Service Health isn't among
that package's supported products,

12
00:00:29.874 --> 00:00:34.812
so the project has nothing to read, and
relies on the provider's other channels.

13
00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:40.374
Answer c is the trap this module is about:
an empty list doesn't mean no incidents.

14
00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:42.802
The module page has three more questions,

15
00:00:42.802 --> 00:00:45.360
each linked to the
section that answers it.
